Feature: Epic 106 Supply Chain Carbon Footprint Tracking
  As an ESG Compliance Officer or Sustainability Manager
  I want a carbon footprint collection engine and automated emission strategies
  So that I can achieve carbon neutrality targets and meet ESG disclosure requirements

  @US-106-01 @ESG @Carbon
  Scenario: Automated carbon footprint data collection across the supply chain
    Given a series of logistics and production activities
    When the carbon engine calculates emissions based on ISO 14064 standards
    Then it must automatically aggregate data from suppliers, transportation, and field operations
    And provide a "Real-time Carbon Dashboard" showing emission intensity per KG of product

  @US-106-02 @AI @Sustainability
  Scenario: AI-driven carbon reduction strategies and ROI calculation
    Given current emission hotspots identified in the supply chain
    When the "ai.decision.engine" analyzes alternatives (e.g. low-carbon logistics or organic inputs)
    Then it must recommend specific reduction measures with predicted CO2e savings
    And calculate the "Sustainability ROI" for each proposed strategy

  @US-106-03 @Compliance @Suppliers
  Scenario: Supplier carbon compliance monitoring and scorecards
    Given a procurement process involving multiple suppliers
    When the sustainability manager reviews the "Supplier Carbon Scorecard"
    Then the system must track supplier progress towards emission targets
    And automatically flag non-compliant suppliers based on the "ESG Redline" (Epic 096)
